1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,910
Hi everyone.

2
00:00:03,110 --> 00:00:03,821
In 2021,

3
00:00:03,821 --> 00:00:08,980
Dependabot opened a pull request on an open source HomeKit

4
00:00:08,980 --> 00:00:14,049
library to upgrade BouncyCastle and remove thirteen known

5
00:00:14,049 --> 00:00:15,472
vulnerabilities.

6
00:00:15,472 --> 00:00:17,126
It broke the build.

7
00:00:17,126 --> 00:00:21,992
It sat open for 1,603 days and was closed without being

8
00:00:21,992 --> 00:00:22,611
merged.

9
00:00:22,611 --> 00:00:27,562
Behind our benchmark are ten real security pull requests

10
00:00:27,562 --> 00:00:28,270
like it.

11
00:00:28,270 --> 00:00:30,446
None of them were merged.

12
00:00:31,646 --> 00:00:33,155
Uptake fixes that.

13
00:00:33,155 --> 00:00:36,473
It hands the broken upgrade to IBM Bob,

14
00:00:36,473 --> 00:00:40,302
locked so it can only change production code,

15
00:00:40,302 --> 00:00:44,726
and proves the result before anyone has to trust it.

16
00:00:45,926 --> 00:00:50,105
In the Bob IDE it is one sentence in the Uptake mode.

17
00:00:50,105 --> 00:00:54,507
Bob reads the real failure through Uptake's MCP server,

18
00:00:54,507 --> 00:00:57,869
including the library's own release notes,

19
00:00:57,869 --> 00:01:00,830
and edits only what it is allowed to.

20
00:01:02,030 --> 00:01:04,839
Some fixes are not Bob's to make.

21
00:01:04,839 --> 00:01:07,011
On the Log4Shell upgrade,

22
00:01:07,011 --> 00:01:12,048
forty-three tests died because a companion logging library

23
00:01:12,048 --> 00:01:13,438
was left behind.

24
00:01:13,438 --> 00:01:18,459
Bob may not touch the build file, so it proposed one line,

25
00:01:18,459 --> 00:01:20,278
and Uptake proved it:

26
00:01:20,278 --> 00:01:23,654
sixty-seven of sixty-seven tests green.

27
00:01:24,854 --> 00:01:26,559
Not every case works.

28
00:01:26,559 --> 00:01:28,876
Across eleven real upgrades,

29
00:01:28,876 --> 00:01:33,179
Bob unblocked seven on the first pass, and one more,

30
00:01:33,179 --> 00:01:35,579
the second Log4Shell upgrade,

31
00:01:35,579 --> 00:01:39,468
once it could read the library's release notes.

32
00:01:39,468 --> 00:01:43,934
The three it did not are on the page with their traces.

33
00:01:45,134 --> 00:01:46,466
Without Uptake,

34
00:01:46,466 --> 00:01:51,616
the same Bob edited tests and build files in three of four

35
00:01:51,616 --> 00:01:52,060
runs.

36
00:01:52,060 --> 00:01:56,880
Once it downgraded a logging library to a 2008 release,

37
00:01:56,880 --> 00:01:59,246
and the build still failed.

38
00:02:00,446 --> 00:02:01,670
On one project,

39
00:02:01,670 --> 00:02:06,238
Bob's fix is identical to the one the maintainers wrote.

40
00:02:06,238 --> 00:02:10,502
Every result ships with a receipt anyone can rebuild.

41
00:02:11,702 --> 00:02:15,483
Eight of eleven security upgrades unblocked,

42
00:02:15,483 --> 00:02:20,296
both Log4Shell upgrades among them, every change proven.

43
00:02:20,296 --> 00:02:24,964
Uptake turns a broken Dependabot pull request into one

44
00:02:24,964 --> 00:02:25,742
approval.

45
00:02:26,942 --> 00:02:28,214
Thank you.

